# Alauda language file - English reference / translation template
#
# This file mirrors the built-in English UI strings exactly, and is the source
# text to translate from. Its section and key order matches every shipped
# translation, so the two files can be compared side by side.
#
# To make a translation:
#   1. Copy this file, for example to ja-JP.lng
#   2. Change id= and name= in [AlaudaLanguage]. Leaving id=en makes Alauda
#      refuse the file: "en" is reserved for the built-in English.
#   3. Translate the value to the right of each "=". Leave the keys alone;
#      a key this file does not list cannot be translated.
#   4. Save as UTF-8. Any other encoding loses every value, and the file is
#      then refused for having no usable translations.
#
# Put the finished file in <foobar2000 profile>\languages. Open Folder on the
# Profiles page opens exactly that folder and, after the rescan, reports any
# file that was refused and why, plus any file that is missing strings.
# A complete folder reports nothing.
#
# A value cannot end in a space: every line is trimmed when the file is read.
# About page text and Diagnostics are intentionally English-only.

